steps.body:
A feed handler hands every tick to a strategy in another process, and a pipe copies each one twice, into the kernel and out again, with a system call on each side. On this Mac a round trip through two pipes between two processes took about 4 µs. **Shared memory** maps the same pages of RAM into two processes, so a value one of them stores, the other loads, with no system call at all.

`mmap` with `MAP_SHARED | MAP_ANONYMOUS` makes pages backed by no file, filled with zeros. `MAP_SHARED` is the opposite of the `MAP_PRIVATE` mapping in *Files: Streams, Buffers, and the Disk*: a `fork` after it doesn't copy these pages on write, so parent and child see the same ones:

```cpp
#include <sys/mman.h>
#include <sys/wait.h>
#include <unistd.h>

void* mem = mmap(nullptr, 4096, PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE, MAP_SHARED | MAP_ANONYMOUS, -1, 0);
long* shared = static_cast<long*>(mem);  // one page, shared with every child forked after this
long copied = 0;                         // an ordinary variable, copied on write
std::cout << std::flush;
if (fork() == 0) {
    *shared = 42;
    copied = 42;
    _exit(0);
}
wait(nullptr);
std::cout << "shared " << *shared << ", copied " << copied << '\n';  // shared 42, copied 0
munmap(mem, 4096);
```

Processes that weren't forked from one another, like a feed handler and a strategy that a supervisor started, find shared memory by name:

1. `shm_open("/ticks", O_CREAT | O_RDWR, 0600)` from `<sys/mman.h>` creates a **shared memory object**, or opens one that exists, and returns a file descriptor. `0600`, in octal, lets only its owner read and write it.
2. `ftruncate(fd, size)` gives a new object its size.
3. `mmap` with `MAP_SHARED` maps it, and every process that maps the name sees the same bytes.
4. `shm_unlink("/ticks")` removes the name. The memory goes once no process maps it.

An object outlives the processes that use it, until `shm_unlink` or a reboot, so a restarted process maps it again and finds its data. On Linux the objects are files in RAM under `/dev/shm`, and a Mac keeps names to 31 characters. Windows names a mapping with `CreateFileMapping` and maps it with `MapViewOfFile`.

Only plain numbers and arrays of them belong in shared memory. Each process may map it at a different address, so a pointer stored there means nothing to the other side, and a `std::string` or `std::vector` holds a pointer into its own process's heap. Two processes writing the same variable at once is a **data race**: their writes can interleave and lose updates, as *Threads, Data Races, and Mutexes*, in the Concurrency section, shows with threads. So give each writer fields of its own.

example.code:
#include <fcntl.h>
#include <sys/mman.h>
#include <sys/wait.h>
#include <unistd.h>
#include <cstdint>
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <vector>

struct Trip {  // one round trip: bought, then sold
    std::string symbol;
    int64_t qty, buy, sell;  // prices in ticks
};

struct Result {  // what a worker leaves in shared memory: plain numbers only
    int64_t pnl;
    int64_t trips;
};

// Creates a shared memory object under a name nothing else is using, and returns its descriptor.
int create_unique(std::string& name) {
    int fd = -1;
    for (int i = 0; fd < 0 && i < 1000; ++i) {
        name = "/backtest-" + std::to_string(getpid()) + "-" + std::to_string(i);
        fd = shm_open(name.c_str(), O_CREAT | O_EXCL | O_RDWR, 0600);  // fails if the name exists
    }
    return fd;
}

int main() {
    const std::vector<std::string> symbols = {"AAPL", "MSFT", "NVDA"};
    const std::vector<Trip> trips = {{"AAPL", 100, 19275, 19281}, {"MSFT", 50, 41010, 41002},
                                     {"AAPL", 200, 19280, 19279}, {"NVDA", 30, 90150, 90190},
                                     {"MSFT", 80, 41000, 41012}, {"AAPL", 100, 19270, 19276}};
    const std::size_t size = symbols.size() * sizeof(Result);
    std::string name;
    const int fd = create_unique(name);
    if (fd < 0) {
        return 1;  // no free name, so nothing was created
    }
    void* mem = MAP_FAILED;
    if (ftruncate(fd, size) == 0) {
        mem = mmap(nullptr, size, PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE, MAP_SHARED, fd, 0);
    }
    close(fd);  // the mapping keeps the object open
    if (mem == MAP_FAILED) {
        shm_unlink(name.c_str());  // every way out after the create removes the name
        return 1;
    }
    Result* results = static_cast<Result*>(mem);  // zero-filled to start

    std::cout << std::flush;
    std::vector<pid_t> workers;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < symbols.size(); ++i) {
        const pid_t pid = fork();
        if (pid == 0) {  // worker i writes only results[i], so no two processes share a field
            for (const Trip& t : trips) {
                if (t.symbol == symbols[i]) {
                    results[i].pnl += t.qty * (t.sell - t.buy);
                    ++results[i].trips;
                }
            }
            _exit(0);
        }
        workers.push_back(pid);
    }
    for (pid_t pid : workers) {
        waitpid(pid, nullptr, 0);  // every worker is done before the parent reads
    }
    int64_t total = 0;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < symbols.size(); ++i) {
        std::cout << symbols[i] << ": trips " << results[i].trips << ", pnl " << results[i].pnl << '\n';
        total += results[i].pnl;
    }
    std::cout << "total pnl " << total << " ticks\n";
    munmap(mem, size);
    shm_unlink(name.c_str());  // removes the name: the memory goes when nothing maps it
    return 0;
}

